(6346256, 938351, 37965, '<td valign="top">WOOOO HOOOO! So psyched about my first ribbon! and breaking 7.0!<br/> <br/>This was taken at a lake in Perryville, AR.  Not Flag Lake, Here is a link to the exact location: <a href="//maps.google.com/maps?q=http:%2F%2Ftrackmytour.com%2F3774.kml&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;source=embed&amp;ll=37.926868,-95.800781&amp;spn=5.510722,13.31543&amp;z=6" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">google map</a> <br/> <br/>I tried applying the rule of thirds here but I liked the centered composition so much better... Rules are meant to be broken!<br/> <br/>Thanks everyone for the comments and votes!  and please check out <a href="//www.giveabike.com" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">giveabike.com</a> <br/><a href="//www.giveabike.blogspot.com" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"> <br/>Give a Bike Blog</a> <br/> <br/>and "like" us on facebook!! <br/> <br/>oh... one correction... this image was taken with the 70-200 4.0 lens not 2.8 IS</td>', 'WOOOO HOOOO! So psyched about my first ribbon! and breaking 7.0! This was taken at a lake in Perryville, AR.  Not Flag Lake, Here is a link to the exact location: google map  I tried applying the rule of thirds here but I liked the centered composition so much better... Rules are meant to be broken! Thanks everyone for the comments and votes!  and please check out giveabike.com  Give a Bike Blog  and "like" us on facebook!!  oh... one correction... this image was taken with the 70-200 4.0 lens not 2.8 IS', '2011-03-09 00:42:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(6346264, 937735, 128304, '<td valign="top">I guess i was the only one who said WOW when they seen this photo, i dont get it? any help....</td>', 'I guess i was the only one who said WOW when they seen this photo, i dont get it? any help....', '2011-03-09 00:44:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(6346276, 938351, 114285, '<td valign="top">Truly deserved.</td>', 'Truly deserved.', '2011-03-09 00:56:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(6346278, 937968, 110108, '<td valign="top">@Janine : setup is pretty simple, I used a 30mm extension tube. Setup the camera on tripod. used a syring to get water dropelets and kept an object, whose refraction you wish to see in the following order.<br/> <br/>Camera -- syring--flower<br/> <br/> * Maintain distance between flower and camera such that you see a good brokeh ( approx 1 feet ).<br/> * Put the syring in between where focus is.<br/> * Press syring to get water slowly and keep pressing the shutter.<br/> * If you have someone else holding the syring, it would be better.<br/></td>', '@Janine : setup is pretty simple, I used a 30mm extension tube. Setup the camera on tripod. used a syring to get water dropelets and kept an object, whose refraction you wish to see in the following order. Camera -- syring--flower  * Maintain distance between flower and camera such that you see a good brokeh ( approx 1 feet ). * Put the syring in between where focus is. * Press syring to get water slowly and keep pressing the shutter. * If you have someone else holding the syring, it would be better.', '2011-03-09 01:01:33.000000', NULL, 0),
