(6346936, 937963, 102315, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by inshaala:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by SEG:</b></div><hr/><i> Absolutely beautiful image. Colors are sooooo vivid. What kind of processing did you use here? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks. Nothing out of the ordinary - it was a lightroom conversion so there was some vibrancy added i suppose.  Most of the colour was present in the first place (food dye fed to a split stem over a couple of days). </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Aha, food dye and a split stem. I remember doing this in school once but have long forgotten that it could be done. I will have to try that. Thanks for the explanation!!!</td>', 'Originally posted by inshaala: Originally posted by SEG: Absolutely beautiful image. Colors are sooooo vivid. What kind of processing did you use here?   Thanks. Nothing out of the ordinary - it was a lightroom conversion so there was some vibrancy added i suppose.  Most of the colour was present in the first place (food dye fed to a split stem over a couple of days).   Aha, food dye and a split stem. I remember doing this in school once but have long forgotten that it could be done. I will have to try that. Thanks for the explanation!!!', '2011-03-09 13:06:06.000000', NULL, 0),
